    "projects.p1Title": "Community Center",
    "projects.p1Location": "Küçükçekmece, Istanbul, Turkey",
    "projects.p1Postcode": "post code 34290",
    "projects.p1Desc": "This project proposes a community centre that strengthens social interaction and community engagement within the neighbourhood. Responding to the site's topography, urban connections, and surrounding land uses, the design transforms a solid building mass into interconnected public and semi-private spaces. The centre includes a library, exhibition areas, workshops, a café, a gym, and multi-purpose halls organised around open courtyards and communal spaces. By combining cultural, educational, and recreational activities, the project creates an inclusive destination that promotes community well-being and everyday social interaction.",

    "projects.p2Title": "Complex Building",
    "projects.p2Location": "Maçka, Istanbul, Turkey",
    "projects.p2Postcode": "post code 34367",
    "projects.p2Desc": "This project proposes a mixed-use accommodation complex that responds to the site's topography, urban context, and surrounding views while balancing public and private spaces. The design evolves from a simple building mass through a series of strategic additions and subtractions that enhance daylight, circulation, and visual connectivity. Following the natural slope of the site, the stepped form creates terraces, semi-open spaces, and communal areas that encourage social interaction. By combining residential units with shared facilities such as study spaces, workshops, cafés, and recreational areas, the project creates a vibrant living environment that fosters community, comfort, and a strong connection to the landscape.",

    "projects.p3Title": "Architectural School",
    "projects.p3Location": "Bomonti, Istanbul, Turkey",
    "projects.p3Postcode": "post code 34381",
    "projects.p3Desc": "This project proposes an Architectural School designed as a dynamic environment for learning, collaboration, and community engagement. The concept is inspired by the spine, with the building's structural framework remaining visible and acting as the main organising element. Similar to a spine, academic and social spaces are connected to this central core, creating a clear spatial hierarchy and strong visual connections throughout the building. The school accommodates studios, classrooms, workshops, digital labs, a library, and exhibition spaces, organised around open circulation routes and shared learning environments. By combining education with public interaction, the project fosters creativity, collaboration, and the exchange of ideas.",

    "projects.w1Title": "Architenko Office",
    "projects.w1Location": "Brussels, Belgium",
    "projects.w1Desc": "During a 90-day internship in Architenko Office, I contributed to the design and technical development of architectural projects through the creation of entrance gate designs, building components, 3D models, and technical documentation. In addition, I conducted supplier and factory research to identify cost-effective manufacturing solutions for project components. This experience enhanced my skills in architectural detailing, technical design, and project coordination.",

    "projects.w2Title": "Farkhan Office",
    "projects.w2Location": "Iran",
    "projects.w2Desc": "Worked on both the design and construction phases of architectural projects within a private architectural practice. Responsibilities included construction supervision of ongoing building projects, reviewing construction details and connections, participating in material selection, and coordinating with site teams. In parallel, I contributed to conceptual and schematic design development, producing architectural diagrams, design studies, and presentation materials. This experience strengthened my understanding of the integration of architectural design with real-world construction processes.",

    "projects.u1Title": "High Level Bridge",
    "projects.u1Location": "Newcastle upon Tyne, UK",
    "projects.u1Postcode": "post code NE8 2AW",
    "projects.u1Desc": "This project proposes an urban design strategy that reconnects Newcastle and Gateshead through the revitalisation of the historic High Level Bridge and its surrounding riverfront. The design focuses on improving pedestrian and cycling connectivity, activating underused green spaces, and creating a vibrant cultural corridor that links heritage landmarks, public spaces, libraries, and recreational areas. Through interventions such as green infrastructure, temporary markets, outdoor learning spaces, cultural activities, and enhanced public routes, the project transforms neglected urban spaces into safe, active, and accessible destinations. By combining heritage preservation, environmental sustainability, and community engagement, the proposal aims to strengthen social interaction, improve spatial justice, and create a memorable urban experience along the River Tyne.",

    "projects.u2Title": "Newburn",
    "projects.u2Location": "Newcastle upon Tyne, UK",
    "projects.u2Postcode": "post code NE15 8NY",
    "projects.u2Desc": "This project proposes an alternative housing development for a 51-hectare riverside site, addressing flooding, affordability, and sustainable growth. Guided by the principle of \"flow with water, not against it,\" the design combines flood-resilient housing with a mix of private, affordable, social, and co-housing models. Green corridors, community spaces, and nature-based water management strategies are integrated to create a resilient and inclusive neighbourhood that promotes social interaction, environmental sustainability, and long-term adaptability.",

    "projects.u3Title": "Ouseburn",
    "projects.u3Location": "Newcastle upon Tyne, UK",
    "projects.u3Postcode": "post code NE6 1LH",
    "projects.u3Desc": "This project proposes a design-code-led regeneration strategy for a former industrial riverside site, transforming it into a vibrant mixed-use destination while preserving its industrial heritage. Guided by the principles of ecological connectivity, industrial identity, and creative diversity, the design introduces cultural spaces, creative workspaces, community facilities, and active public areas that respond to the site's existing character. Green corridors, pedestrian and cycling routes, and riverside public spaces strengthen connections across the site and improve accessibility. By adapting existing structures and integrating landscape and heritage assets, the project creates a distinctive and sustainable environment that supports community engagement and long-term urban regeneration.",

    "projects.uw1Title": "MawsonKerr Office",
    "projects.uw1Location": "Newcastle upon Tyne, UK",
    "projects.uw1Desc": "Collaborated in a design workshop focused on transforming an underused urban space into an inclusive and vibrant temporary public space. Contributed to site analysis, concept development, spatial design, and presentation materials while working closely with a multidisciplinary team.",

    "projects.uw2Title": "Ryder Office",
    "projects.uw2Location": "Newcastle upon Tyne, UK",
    "projects.uw2Desc": "Completed a short-term internship at an architecture firm, participating in urban design and masterplanning projects from initial research and analysis through to design and final presentation. Responsibilities included case study analysis, project brief development, site analysis, spatial planning, massing studies, and design concept development.\n\nAdditionally, developed 3D models of projects using Revit and prepared drawings, presentation materials, visual imagery, renders, and portfolio content to effectively communicate design ideas.\n\nThis experience provided a comprehensive understanding of the professional urban design process, from contextual studies and concept formation to development, presentation, and effective communication of design ideas.",

